  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">💶 Who is saving for pension in Europe?

As shown in the third edition of the Household Report, published last July, the extent to which households save for retirement is one of the most important factors helping to explain their participation in capital markets. The high level of pension fund savings in several European countries reflects long-lasting policy efforts to achieve high coverage of funded pensions through mandatory or quasi-mandatory arrangements.

📊 The visual below highlights how five European countries — the Netherlands, Sweden, the United Kingdom, Norway and Denmark — stand out significantly from the rest of Europe in terms of pension fund savings per capita.

