  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">🛠️ In part 4 of our LinkedIn series discussing MISP and cross-border UCITS, we assess the parts of the proposal that could benefit from further improvement. The current proposal already does a good job at improving cross-border distribution of UCITS. However, if EU competitiveness and regulatory simplification are the goals, there is more we can do to remove complexity and avoid new rules that are unclear in practice. Now is the perfect opportunity.

This includes:
🔹 Simple, standardised fund authorisation documents that avoid duplications.
🔹 Keeping compliance checks on marketing materials AFTER authorisation.
🔹 Some flexibility in harmonised marketing requirements.
🔹 Clarifying what a ‘material’ change to a fund is, while also simplifying notification of these.
🔹 No duplicative supervisory fees for the same procedure or service.
🔹 No Member State requirements to maintain a physical presence in the ‘host’ jurisdiction.

📑 One thing MISP does not address is various national reporting requirements imposed by some Member States. This often adds a huge amount of unnecessary paperwork for fund managers. However, ESMA’s plans for an integrated fund reporting system could eliminate these, which would greatly reduce complexity. This is where real improvements in the supervision of EU asset management can be made, not a single EU supervisor or annual reviews of large cross-border entities by ESMA.

We will have more about this soon!

👉 You can find our full position on the MISP here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eTRBhsDU?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eTRBhsDU</a>

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fucits&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#UCITS</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Ffundpassport&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#fundpassport</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsinglemarket&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#SingleMarket</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fmisp&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#MISP</a></p>
